[statement]
A provided name's single candidate stating two entries on one name has
that name decided on the first before the candidate is installed: `v`'s
one candidate `p1` needs `lib>0` and then `lib<2`; apk installs `lib` 2.0
and cannot install `p1` beside it, and refuses. Requested by its own name,
`p1` gets `lib` 1.0. Observed; the rule is not yet known.

[repository]
P:app
V:1
D:v

P:p1
V:1
p:v=1
D:lib>0 lib<2

P:lib
V:1.0

P:lib
V:2.0

[request]
app

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   lib-2.0:
|     breaks: p1-1[lib<2]
|     satisfies: p1-1[lib>0]
refused
